---
title: 'Ecological Restoration in Nepal: A Comprehensive Policy Overview'
authors: Pant, R. R., Koirala, M., Adhikari, D., & Gaire, N. P.
year: '2024'
category: Book Chapter
linkType: doi
doi: https://doi.org/10.1079/9781800622579.0011
abstract: >-
  This chapter presents a comprehensive description of Nepal’s conservation and
  restoration strategies and policies. The goal of the policies is to foster
  sustainable development and safeguard the unique and diverse ecosystems. The
  escalating population has increased the demand for natural resources like
  forestry products, water, land and minerals, which could lead to a degradation
  of ecosystem services. Some restoration projects are improving the ecosystem
  functions and services, but intensive efforts are still needed. By adopting
  ecosystem restoration and resource conservation strategies, Nepal improves
  ecosystem functions and services, and livelihoods. An integrated approach to
  restoration offers additional benefits, creating employment opportunities in
  the country’s post-pandemic economic recovery.
